From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: givethesourceplox <272928635+givethesourceplox@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 10:59:35 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] Scale Ocarina's decoded NDVE movie frames directly on Metal

The title movie shows block corruption after NDVE reconstruction. The
decoded RGBA image is clean before the reconstruction dispatches.

Add an opt-in path that scales that image into the normal movie output
with a bilinear Metal draw. Match the observed shader keys and check the
submission and texture layout before replacing the final dispatch.

Document the switch and add a Metal check for the scaled output and
submission lifetime.

(cherry picked from commit b6367705af06c56243402954686711d09dfa92ba)

Upstream-Status: forwarded seedds/nxnative#1331
Reason: Ocarina of Time's title movie and title screen run at 30 fps with the audio drifting behind the picture without it; upstream has not merged the PR yet
Issue: seedds/nxnative#1375

